# BUG-007 — Last Name Input Is Redirected to First Name Field and Characters Replace Previous Input

## Summary

When logged in as `problem_user`, entering a Last Name during checkout incorrectly places the input into the First Name field. Each newly entered character replaces the previously entered character instead of being appended.

## Environment

| Item | Details |
|------|---------|
| Application | SauceDemo Web Application |
| User | problem_user |
| Browser | Google Chrome |
| Operating System | Windows 11 |
| Test Type | Functional Testing |

## Preconditions

- SauceDemo application is accessible.
- User is logged in as `problem_user`.
- A product has been added to the Shopping Cart.

## Steps to Reproduce

1. Log in using `problem_user`.
2. Add a product to the Shopping Cart.
3. Click Checkout.
4. Enter a valid First Name.
5. Click the Last Name field.
6. Type a Last Name one character at a time.
7. Observe the First Name and Last Name fields.

## Expected Result

- Characters entered in the Last Name field should appear in the Last Name field.
- Characters should be appended sequentially to form the entered value.
- The First Name field should remain unchanged.

## Actual Result

- Characters entered into the Last Name field appear in the First Name field.
- Each newly entered character replaces the previously entered character in the First Name field.
- The Last Name field remains empty.
- The user is unable to enter a valid Last Name and cannot complete checkout.

## Severity

High

